  "reason": "The current best result is config_023 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat) at 0.688 acc, showing that multiprofile + transformer aggregation is the dominant performance driver. In singleprofile, concat and weighted fusion were nearly identical (0.527 vs 0.523), but that comparison was made without multiprofile + transformer aggregation, where the interaction dynamics between modalities may differ. Config_015 is a single-variable change (concat → weighted) from the current best, making it a clean A/B test of the fusion mechanism in the strongest known setup. If weighted fusion helps, it provides a free improvement to the best configuration; if not, it confirms concat is sufficient and redirects the next experiment toward RNA encoder (scgpt) or image encoder (ViT) as the next lever. Under a limited budget, this is the lowest-risk, highest-clarity experiment to either exploit the current best or rule out a design choice before moving to larger architectural changes."
}

